   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614568,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Upon exploring the area, de Soto discovered the Native Americans were primarily engaged in which industry for survival?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166246,
     "content_html": "Agriculture\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166245,
     "content_html": "Herding\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166244,
     "content_html": "Hunting\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166243,
     "content_html": "Slave trade\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614569,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "According to his letter, how did de Soto view the Native Americans he came across?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166250,
     "content_html": "As a good source of information for his army and of food supplies\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166249,
     "content_html": "As people with equal rights\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166248,
     "content_html": "As a civilization not to be disturbed by Europeans\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166247,
     "content_html": "As a potential ally in conquering neighboring lands\n"
    }
   ],
